<title>INDIA: India SBI 96/97 net higher.</title>
<headline>India SBI 96/97 net higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>	  (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	   13,293.0    vs     8,316.0</p>
<p>    Interest income   149,506.6    vs   129,585.7</p>
<p>    Shr (in rupees)	  26.66   vs	  17.54</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	   4.0    vs	   3.5</p>
<p>    Other income	 26,430.7    vs    27,570.2</p>
<p>    Interest costs     95,914.3    vs    82,259.2</p>
<p>    Operating expense  46,046.7    vs    44,595.4</p>
<p>    Provisions*	  20,683.3    vs    21,985.3</p>
<p>Note - State Bank of India, the country's largest commercial bank, said paid-up capital rose to 5.26 billion rupees, from 4.74 billion rupees, after its issue of global depository receipts in October 1996. The latest dividend is payable on the higher capital.</p>
<p>The bank said provisions include contingencies.</p>
<p>SBI's capital adequacy ratio rose to 12.17 percent from 11.6 percent in 1995/96.</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
